-- title:
--   No p-power torsion in the Eichler–Shimura specialisation kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ and let $p$ be a natural number. Let $\ell$ be a prime not dividing $N p$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $\ell$ in the sense that the image of $\ell$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ belongs to the nonunits of $A$. Work in $J :=$ [`ModularCurve.JZero N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L115), the group of degree-zero divisor classes (degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones) of the function field obtained from the full modular function field of level $N$ by base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with its action of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ and the $\mathbb Z$-linear Hecke endomorphism $T_\ell =$ [`ModularCurve.heckeOperatorBar N ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L16). Let $x \in J$ satisfy $p^n \cdot x = 0$ for some $n \in \mathbb N$, and suppose $x$ lies in the additive subgroup of $J$ generated by the union of two sets: the coboundaries $\tau \cdot z - z$, where $\tau$ runs over the image in $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ and $z$ over $J$; and the elements $\sigma \cdot \sigma \cdot z - T_\ell(\sigma \cdot z) + \ell \cdot z$, where $z \in J$ and $\sigma$ is any automorphism lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $y \mapsto y^{\ell}$. Then $x = 0$.
--
--   This is the injectivity half of the good-reduction specialisation statement for $J_0(N)$ at a prime $\ell \nmid Np$: the quotient of $J$ by the subgroup generated by inertia coboundaries and Eichler–Shimura elements is the universal recipient of a specialisation datum at $A$, and the assertion is that the quotient map is injective on $p$-power torsion. It is used to produce such a specialisation datum, in [`ModularCurve.specializationExists_JZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.specializationExists_JZero).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_eq_zero_of_torsion_of_mem_specializationKernel_jZero.lean

import Mathlib
